0..56 Comment "// `Terms(S)` is the type of closed terms of theory `S`."
57..59 Comment "//"
60..121 Comment "// A theory has models. The initial model contains its terms."
122..124 Comment "//"
125..193 Comment "// `Terms(S)` avoids a second declaration for the terms of a theory."
194..268 Comment "// `Terms(S)` derives one data declaration for each theory. Each operation"
269..346 Comment "// gives one constructor. The theory\'s rules orient as the rules of that data"
347..423 Comment "// block, and the presentation check of the block judges them. A fold into a"
424..457 Comment "// model respects the model laws."
458..460 Comment "//"
461..539 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/theory-terms.gandr` — a monoid\'s terms, refused"
540..601 Comment "// - owes: #4148 — the terms as a model, and a derived fold"
602..648 Comment "// - owes: #4149 — a fold over a model value"
649..694 Comment "// - owes: #4150 — terms over several sorts"
695..775 Comment "// - see: `model/identity/loop-winding.gandr` — a fold out of a presented type"
776..800 Comment "//   into a model module"
